    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 372 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Commissions",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4870\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 372 of the laws of 2008, amend-\ning the parks, recreation and historic preservation law relating to\nestablishing the Niagara Falls underground railroad heritage commission,\nin relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: This bill will change the date when\nArticle 43 of the Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation law\nexpires to allow the Commission to initiate implementation of the\nmanagement plan approved pursuant to Article 43 of the Parks, Recreation\nand Historic Preservation law.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: This bill amends Section 3 of Chanter\n372 of the Laws of 2008 to extend Article 43 of the Parks, Recreation\nand Historic Preservation Law to December 31, 2015.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: The Niagara Falls Underground Railroad Heritage Commis-\nsion was designated as part of New York's system of heritage areas in\n2008. The Commission encompasses the City of Niagara Falls, in Niagara\nCounty. The importance of the Commission's mission to develop the herit-\nage corridor to function as a destination for both academic research and\ntourism is imperative. The Commission's management plan was approved by\nthe Commissioner of Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation on duly\n3, 2012. This legislation would give the Niagara Falls Underground Rail-\nroad Heritage Commission additional time to assist local agencies with\nthe initial implementation of the management plan.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: None\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
